# Documentation Conventions

The `docs/` tree is the project's source of truth.

- Write in **clear English**; preserve Arabic business terminology where useful (see `docs/00-project/GLOSSARY.md`).
- Every doc starts with a header block containing **Status** and **Last updated** (YYYY-MM-DD). Update both when editing.
- Every doc contains: purpose, rules/content, and current decisions.
- **Do not invent requirements or fields.** Unresolved decisions are explicitly marked **TBD** — never silently resolved.
- **Documentation must reflect actual behavior. Do not document planned behavior as completed** — module docs describe planned contracts and conceptual models until implemented.
- Never describe future-scope items as part of the current MVP.
- Module documentation lives in `docs/09-modules/<module>/` with: README, BUSINESS_RULES, PERMISSIONS, API, DATA_MODEL, UI, ACCEPTANCE_CRITERIA, TEST_PLAN.
- Every completed feature must update, where relevant: MVP scope status, business rules, API docs, database docs, module docs, CHANGELOG, and an ADR if architecture changed — in the same PR.
- ADRs in `docs/10-decisions/` (`ADR-NNNN-TITLE.md`): Status, Context, Decision, Consequences. Changing an accepted decision requires updating or superseding its ADR.
